TRACE - eBPF tracepoint management

Commands:
  list                              List all available tracepoints
  enable <tp> [--prog NAME]         Enable tracepoint, optionally attach program
  disable <tp>                      Disable a tracepoint
  stat [--hist EVENT] [--top N]    Show probe statistics
  stream [--filter TYPE] [-n N]    Stream events in real-time
  dump [--filter TYPE] [-n N]      Dump buffered events
  verbose [on|off]                  Control real-time eBPF output
  reset                             Reset all statistics
  load file <path> <tp>             Load eBPF program from file and attach
  load prog <id> <tp>               Attach loaded program to tracepoint
  unload <tp>                       Detach program from tracepoint
  progs                             List pre-compiled and loaded programs
  path <prog_id>                    Show axtrace eBPF request paths
  hprobe <symbol> <prog_id>         Attach hprobe to VMM function
  hretprobe <symbol> <prog_id>      Attach hretprobe to VMM function
  unhprobe <symbol>                 Detach hprobe from VMM function
  kprobe vm<id>:<addr|symbol> <prog> Attach kprobe to guest kernel function
  unkprobe vm<id>:<addr|symbol>     Detach kprobe from guest kernel function
  uprobe vm<id>:<path>:<sym> <prog> Attach uprobe to guest userspace function
  unuprobe vm<id>:<path>:<sym>      Detach uprobe from guest userspace function
  loadsyms vm<id> <path>            Load guest symbol file (nm/System.map)
  gsym vm<id> <name|addr>           Query guest symbol by name/address
  uloadelf vm<id> <guest> <path>    Load guest user ELF symbols for uprobe

Pre-compiled programs:
  stats    - Event counter with latency (COUNT/TOTAL/MIN/MAX)
  printk   - Debug logger with count

Examples:
  trace enable vmm:vcpu_run_enter
  trace enable vmm:vcpu_run_exit --prog stats
  trace enable shell:shell_command --prog printk
  trace hprobe axvm::Vm::create 0
  trace verbose on
  trace progs
  trace stat
